  "text": "𬟽 Let's denote the five positive integers as \\( a, b, c, d, \\) and \\( e \\). Each edge of the pyramid is labeled with the sum of the two numbers on the adjacent faces. If the product of the numbers on the edges is equal to 243, we can express this as:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+d)(d+e)(e+a) = 243\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to factorize 243:\n\\[\n243 = 3^5\n\\]\n\nNote that 243 must be represented as a product of five positive integers where each integer is a positive sum of two other integers. To satisfy this, we should check if we can split 243 into five digits where each digit is a positive sum of two other digits:\n\\[\n243 = 9 \\times 9 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nThis splits into forced sums as follows:\n\\[\na+b = 9, \\quad b+c = 9, \\quad c+d = 3, \\quad d+e = 3, \\quad e+a = 3\n\\]\n\nFrom the equations, we have:\n\\[\na+b = 9, \\quad b+c = 9, \\quad c+d = 3, \\quad d+e = 3, \\quad e+a = 3\n\\]\n\nBy summing all equations, we get:\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+d) + (d+e) + (e+a) = 9 + 9 + 3 + 3 + 3\n\\]\n\nThe right side simplifies to:\n\\[\n2a + 2b + 2c + 2d + 2e = 24\n\\]\n\nDividing by 2, we get:\n\\[\na + b + c + d + e = 12\n\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the numbers written on the faces is 12. Therefore, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
